      "side": 1,
      "message": "Debugging with Keith revealed that `GPIO_OUTPUT_INACTIVE` and `GPIO_OUTPUT_ACTIVE` were returning the same values because a prior test had already executed [egis630_init](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis630.c;l\u003d104?q\u003dfingerprint_egis630.c\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d103-,104,-105). This call inadvertently set the reset pin to a logical low state. The issue was resolved by commenting out the logic within the [egis_fp_reset_sensor](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis630.c;l\u003d53?q\u003dfingerprint_egis630.c\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d52-,53,-54) function, which allowed the expected behavior to be observed.\n\nI am going to resolve this comment as the behavior is fully understood.",
